////FUTURE////

MIXED DML OPERATION Error - When we create both the objects togather  in same transaction Setup object (User , Group etc) and Non Setup object(account contact etc)
Any object that affects salesforce security like User etc. is a setup object , in case of User object on updating certain fields triggers this exception 
eg. Role Id

To overcome this error we use future method
Puts the method in Flex Queue - So not considerd as synchronous calling so no MIXED DML OPERATION Error
@future annotation
only primitive data type accepted not sobject type , no return , public static or global method
If the method is making a callout then the method must have @future(callout =true)

in devconsole we see the log as futureHandler , this method has to be evaluated in dev console don't gives any UI errors

Future Limitations
1.Can not pass sObject or List<sObject> as a method parameter
2. Can not call future from future OR We can not chain future method (cant track as dont return any job id , not sure when will it run in flex queue)
3. We can not monitor future method because it does not return any Job Id
4. Future methods best work for the small size of records. 10 OR 20 Records
5. There can be only 50 future methods in a Single Transaction 

////QUEUABLE////

1. Its a class that implements System.Queueable interface , need
2. we can call furure from queable , we can chain queueable , 
3. queable accepts all data typesa as well becaue it is a class , and class has constructor in which we can pass the parameters of diff type
5. it also has possibility of data loss so use the ids and fetch data
6. Every queable apex comes with a freh set of governer limits while in Syncronous methods its 6 MB heap size , 10 S CPU time out , 100 SOQL Queries and
    150 DML statements
7. output of first job can be passed to the input of second JOB with the help of constructor
8. we can call 1 queueable form another then another 1 from previous one and so on , for dev org this limit is 5 for more than this the error comes
|FATAL_ERROR|System.AsyncException: Maximum stack depth has been reached.


////BATCH/////

Future-Small set of records 10-20, 50
Queable - 5k,10k records , pass 1 output to other

BATCH- Process large amount of data , 50 million , fetching datafrom external system , highrst set of governer limits
Database.batchable<sObject> interface , avalilable in Database NAMESPACE
  has 3 methods - START - Only onec and will always execute, fetch records and pass to execute , using 2 classes
                            Database.QueryLocator (QueryLocator class in Database namespace)
                            Database.Iterator (Iterator class in Datatabase Namespace)
                                      We have to create a custom iterator
                                      can process ony 50K records as SOQL allows only that many
                  EXECUTE - run if it has records , heart of batch
                            Business Logic
                  FINISH - Only Once and will always execute
                            Perform cleanup logic , sending email , calling another batch apex

Default batch size is 200 , maximum 2000 , minimum 1 
if start method is iterator then no upper limit

////Batch Job Status

Holding - submitted to flex , waiting for resources
Queued - resources now available , waiting for execution
Preparing - start method
Processing - execute method
Aborted - Aborted by user or form apex
Completed - Completed without faliure
Failed - Job experienced system faliure

Id jobid = Database.executeBach(instance of batch apex);
Id jobid = Database.executeBach(instance of batch apex,batch size);

No of execute method calls = No.of records/Chunk Size
Each execute call has its own governer limits
for a set of records if 1 exceute call fails then the other call containg next set of records can process successfully
they are not related to each other

If we create a batch class for one object and query records related to that object  but pass other type object in execute method
then the bath will not give any output

Database.executeBatch cant be called from a batch start , batch execute or future method
        
For chanining of batch calsses we nedd to call the Database.executeBatch  in finish method

Queable can be called from Start , Finish or execute method of a batch class but we should avoid calling it from execute
as execute is called may times and it can shoot flex queue limits

Batch can be called from queueables as well

//////Database.Stateful interface

Maintains the state of batch instance variables, means it keeps the value of class,instance variables in alll 3 methods same i.e
Start,Execute,Finish , as these methods are not connected and run in seprate threads so the values of class variables are not
maintained across methods
So we use Database.Stateful interface in the class to maintain the state of variables

Database.Stateful  is a marker interface as it has no methods

